{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CFu4z279cUNoFYf4zbptJB","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/ROADMAP.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# recovery_aware_struct_prune — Research Dashboard\\\\n\\\\n> 最后更新: 2026-05-15 14:50 UTC | 更新原因: D032 GRPO v8 双卡稳定运行，更新工程历史和任务状态\\\\n\\\\n## 核心方向\\\\nRecovery-Aware Structured Pruning (RASP)：CKA functional overlap 指导结构化剪枝，在 matched sparsity 下比 importance-only 剪枝显著更好地保留推理能力（**Redundancy Paradox**）。详见 paper_framing.md。\\\\n\\\\n## 目标会议\\\\nEMNLP 2026 ARR May 25 提交（距今 10 天）\\\\n\\\\n## 当前阶段\\\\n**Research Phase** — GRPO v8 双卡稳定运行中（D032）。westd GraSP SFT + α ablation 并行推进。\\\\n\\\\n## 核心证据（D027 修正后）\\\\n- ~~Post-prune: RASP 29% vs Standard 1%~~ → **D027 修正: RASP 31% vs Standard 27% (4pp, p=0.54, 不显著)**\\\\n- Post-SFT GSM8K (N=100): RASP 57% vs Standard 64%（Standard 反超 7pp）\\\\n- GraSP post-prune: 8% — RASP >> GraSP 3.6x，gradient-based baseline 远劣（D027 仍成立）\\\\n- α ablation post-prune: α=0.0 30% / α=0.5 25% / α=1.0 27% / α=4.0 40%（CI 重叠，N=100 不足以区分）\\\\n- α=4.0 post-SFT: 62%，α=1.0 post-SFT: 57%——SFT 有均衡化效应\\\\n- **GRPO v8 是唯一尚存的核心假设验证路径**\\\\n\\\\n## Claims & 实验覆盖\\\\n| Claim | P0 实验 | 状态 |\\\\n|-------|---------|------|\\\\n| C1: CKA-aware pruning preserves reasoning | plan_001-006, plan_015 | ⏳ GRPO v8 运行中 |\\\\n| C2: F(h) predicts recoverability | plan_007-008, plan_014-015 | 待 GRPO 完成 |\\\\n| C3: Recovery method conditions pruning order | plan_009 | SFT: Standard>RASP (D029)；待 GRPO 确认反转 |\\\\n\\\\n## 近期任务\\\\n- [ ] **GRPO v8 双卡运行中** — westb cuda:0 RASP, cuda:1 Standard (~21h, ETA ~5/16 11:30 UTC)\\\\n- [ ] **GRPO v8 监控** — step 5 (~1h) 和 step 20 (~4h) 检查 reward/grad_norm 早期信号\\\\n- [ ] **GraSP SFT + eval** — westd cuda:0，接近完成\\\\n- [ ] **α ablation SFT sweep** — westd cuda:1, 已完成 α=0.0/0.5/1.0/4.0, α=2.0 启动中\\\\n- [ ] GRPO v8 完成 → eval 两模型(N=100, greedy) → 判定: |RASP-Standard| >15pp/5-15pp/<5pp\\\\n- [ ] 全部 α SFT+eval 完成 → α vs recovery 曲线\\\\n- [ ] [Dream P0] α ablation plan_015 — GRPO 完成后立即执行\\\\n- [ ] [Dream P1] Inference speedup plan_016 / Unstructured baseline plan_017\\\\n- [ ] [Dream] Multi-seed 扩展 plan_006 到 5 seeds\\\\n- [x] D027 definitive re-eval: RASP 31% vs Standard 27%\\\\n- [x] D028 kill v5 → start v6 (512→1024 fix truncation)\\\\n- [x] D029 SFT recovery: Standard 64% > RASP 57%\\\\n- [x] GraSP post-prune: 8%\\\\n- [x] D032 GRPO v8 启动（v6 OOM → v7 磁盘满 → v8 修复缓存+GPU映射+参数）\\\\n\\\\n## GRPO 结果 Contingency\\\\n| GRPO 结果 | 影响 | 行动 |\\\\n|-----------|------|------|\\\\n| RASP >> Standard (>15pp) | Recovery-pathway hypothesis 成立 | 全面推进 plan_001-017，story: CKA-guided pruning 创造更好 RL recovery dynamics |\\\\n| RASP > Standard (5-15pp) | Claim 1 成立但需加固 | 优先 plan_001 full eval + plan_006 multi-seed + plan_015 α ablation |\\\\n| RASP ≈ Standard (<5pp) | 核心假设失败 | 根本性 pivot: 转 training dynamics 分析 / 25% sparsity / 负向发现论文 |\\\\n| Standard > RASP | 全面失败 | Reframe 或终止 |\\\\n\\\\n## GPU 预算\\\\n- **westb-23072**: 2× ~98GB GPU | cuda:0 GRPO RASP v8, cuda:1 GRPO Standard v8\\\\n- **westd-11672**: 2× ~95GB GPU | cuda:0 GraSP SFT+eval, cuda:1 α ablation SFT sweep\\\\n- 约束 C001: 仅允许 westb cuda:0/1, westd cuda:0/1\\\\n- 总预算 ~480 GPU-hours (10 days × 2 server × 2 GPU × 24h)\\\\n\\\\n## GRPO 工程问题历史（v1-v8）\\\\nv1-v4: 截断/collapse/ETA过长 → v5: step 80 collapse → v6: OOM step 8 → v7: 磁盘满+参数错误+重复进程 → **v8: 缓存迁移+GPU映射+参数统一，双卡稳定运行**\\\\n\\\\n## 论文写作备忘（Dream 通用建议，给 Paper Agent）\\\\n- 扩展 references 到 25+，引用 FANG、FuncNet、RestoreLCC、PAT\\\\n- 论证 CKA vs SVCCA/CCA/MI 选择\\\\n- 讨论 Claim 2 潜在循环性并加以区分\\\\n- 报告 I(h)-F(h) correlation\\\\n- Temper scope claims（单模型局限性坦诚讨论）\\\\n\\\\n## 关键风险\\\\n1. **GRPO v8 失败 = 项目需根本性 pivot**——唯一核心风险\\\\n2. Post-prune 差异仅 4pp (p=0.54)——pre-recovery claim 已不成立，论文 story 完全依赖 GRPO recovery 阶段差异\\\\n3. 单模型限制 → Dream 三档一致标记\\\\n4. DDL 10 天——GRPO 结果 5/16 出，留 ~9 天写作+补实验\\\\n\\\\n## 关键决策日志\\\\n\\\\n| ID | 日期 | 摘要 | 关联实验 |\\\\n|----|------|------|----------|\\\\n| D032 | 2026-05-15 | GRPO v7 双组崩溃(磁盘满+静默死亡)，v8 修复: HF cache 迁移数据盘 + GPU | grpo_stage2_rasp_20_v7, grpo_stage2_standard_20_v7 |\\\\n| D031 | 2026-05-15 | GRPO v6 OOM at step 8, 切 v7: 8-bit AdamW optimizer | grpo_stage2_rasp_20_v6, grpo_stage2_standard_20_v6 |\\\\n| D030 | 2026-05-15 | GRPO v6 双卡 OOM 崩溃(step 8)，切 v7: 8-bit optimizer +  | grpo_stage2_rasp_20_v6, grpo_stage2_standard_20_v6 |\\\\n| D029 | 2026-05-15 | SFT recovery 阶段 Standard 优于 RASP/α=4.0，核心假设在 SFT 层 | sft_alpha4_0_westd, sft_standard_20_retrain, grpo_stage2_rasp_20_v6, grpo_stage2_standard_20_v6 |\\\\n| D028 | 2026-05-15 | Kill GRPO v5 (RASP+Standard)，切 v6: max_completion_ | grpo_stage2_rasp_20_v5, grpo_stage2_standard_20_v5 |\\\\n| D027 | 2026-05-15 | Post-prune 核心 claim 崩塌（RASP 31% vs Standard 27%, p | reeval_postprune_definitive, grpo_stage2_rasp_20_v5 |\\\\n| D026 | 2026-05-15 | 将 RASP definitive re-eval 部署到 westd GPU 0 并行执行，不等  | reeval_postprune_definitive |\\\\n| D025 | 2026-05-15 | 挂起 D006/D014 基于 \\\\\\\"29x advantage\\\\\\\" 的所有结论，等待 definitiv | D023, D006, D014 |\\\\n| D024 | 2026-05-15 | CRITICAL: D023 re-eval 显示 Standard post-prune ~32% | D023, alpha_ablation_phase_a |\\\\n| D023 | 2026-05-15 | α ablation Phase A 暴露 importance formula confound  | alpha_ablation_phase_a |\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 4626, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JjoCkoWmGvH77iEv5CoXPc","session_id":"e50da390-5c7e-4dcd-8358-bec3c8329c08","uuid":"8f5353a2-e181-43d2-9d9a-962978de8ec1","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:59:53.875Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FWZyEC6hmEu1orHZWS6ASp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019tsg4NcztGqR1zjUepgBdd","name":"mcp__agent-ml-research__read_project_file","input":{"project":"recovery_aware_struct_prune","file":"paper_framing.md","max_chars":0},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2300,"cache_read_input_tokens":16965,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2300,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":70,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JjoCkoWmGvH77iEv5CoXPc","session_id":"e50da390-5c7e-4dcd-8358-bec3c8329c08","uuid":"39d4a07a-03b4-4102-8071-0e9ff2e69bc0"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019tsg4NcztGqR1zjUepgBdd","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/paper_framing.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Paper Framing — recovery_aware_struct_prune\\\\n\\\\n## Target Venue\\\\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25 submission)\\\\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\\\\n- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026\\\\n\\\\n## Core Insight (Redundancy Paradox)\\\\nTraditional structured pruning selects structures to remove based on importance metrics alone (weight magnitude, gradient sensitivity). We show this misses a critical signal for RLVR recovery: **functional uniqueness**. Structures with high functional overlap (high CKA) can be safely pruned because RLVR redistributes their function across retained structures. Structures with low overlap are functionally irreplaceable — once removed, even RLVR cannot recreate their unique contribution. This creates a **Redundancy Paradox**: protecting functionally unique structures matters more for recovery than protecting high-importance structures.\\\\n\\\\nRASP exploits this via S(h) = I(h) × (1-F(h))^α: high overlap → low score → **pruned first**; low overlap → high score → **protected**. The result: RASP preferentially removes functionally redundant structures (whose function RLVR can recover) while Standard pruning may accidentally remove functionally unique structures that happen to have low importance scores. At 20% sparsity, this effect manifests entirely within MLP channel groups (0/112 attention GQA groups are pruned under either method; all 200 pruned structures are MLP groups), consistent with the \\\\\\\"RL Squeezes, SFT Expands\\\\\\\" mechanism (ICLR 2026).\\\\n\\\\n## Core Claims (3)\\\\n\\\\n1. **CKA-aware pruning enables superior RLVR recovery**: At matched sparsity and parameter count, RASP and Standard pruning yield comparable post-prune accuracy (31% vs 27% GSM8K at 20% sparsity, N=100, p=0.54 — D027 corrected), but diverge dramatically after RLVR recovery. The decisive evidence is the GRPO recovery gap (v7 running), not post-prune accuracy. If confirmed, this means CKA-aware structure selection preserves reasoning scaffolding that RLVR can leverage, even when immediate accuracy is similar.\\\\n\\\\n2. **Functional overlap predicts per-structure recoverability** *(scope: MLP channel groups at moderate sparsity)*: Per-structure CKA functional overlap F(h) is a stronger predictor of post-recovery accuracy retention than standard importance metrics alone, within the MLP channel groups that are actually pruned at 20-25% sparsity. At these sparsity levels, attention GQA groups consistently rank above all MLP groups in the global importance list (0/112 pruned); the CKA signal's practical effect is selecting *which* MLP groups to prune (N=784, ~200 pruned). Validated via mixed-effects regression (layer as random effect) on MLP groups, controlling for weight norm, gradient importance, and activation magnitude. Cross-component (attention + MLP) validation requires higher sparsity (~40%+).\\\\n\\\\n3. **Recovery method conditions optimal pruning order**: The relative ranking of pruning strategies changes depending on recovery method (RLVR vs SFT). Structures expendable under RLVR recovery may be critical under SFT recovery, consistent with the \\\\\\\"RL Squeezes, SFT Expands\\\\\\\" mechanism — RLVR compresses incorrect paths (tolerates removal of overlapping structures) while SFT expands correct paths (needs preserved trajectory-encoding structures).\\\\n\\\\n## Story Spine\\\\n\\\\n- **Problem**: Structured pruning for reasoning LLMs optimizes for immediate post-pruning accuracy, treating subsequent recovery as independent. But post-prune accuracy is a poor proxy for recoverability: two pruning strategies can yield similar immediate accuracy (31% vs 27%) yet produce dramatically different outcomes after RLVR recovery. The choice of *which structures* to prune — not just how many — determines whether recovery can succeed.\\\\n\\\\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Self-Healing (2025) shows RLVR recovers pruned reasoning models to 95%+ at 25% compression but uses standard pruning and tests only one ratio. GRASPrune (ACL 2026) provides SOTA budgeted structural pruning but doesn't study reasoning-specific recovery. RESP (Dec 2025) uses reasoning-trace calibration but has no recovery phase. No work studies how the pruning structure choice interacts with RLVR recovery quality, or whether optimal pruning differs for RLVR vs SFT recovery.\\\\n\\\\n- **Our framing**: We introduce Recovery-Aware Structured Pruning (RASP), reframing structural redundancy from a flaw to eliminate into a signal of RLVR recoverability. RASP scores structures by S(h) = I(h) × (1 - F(h))^α, protecting functionally unique reasoning scaffolding while allowing removal of structures whose function can be redistributed through RLVR. This connects to the Lottery Ticket Hypothesis at a new level: LTH asks \\\\\\\"which subnetwork trains well\\\\\\\" (binary); RASP asks \\\\\\\"which structures to remove so the remainder recovers well under a specific training paradigm\\\\\\\" (paradigm-conditioned trainability).\\\\n\\\\n- **Headline result template**: \\\\\\\"At 20% structured sparsity on DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B, RASP and Standard pruning achieve comparable post-prune accuracy (31% vs 27%), yet RASP enables RLVR recovery to X% while Standard recovers only to Y% (Δ=Z pp, p<0.01). Post-prune accuracy is a poor predictor of recoverability; CKA-based functional overlap explains W% of per-structure recovery variance (mixed-effects β, p < 0.001).\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n## Venue Fit\\\\n- EMNLP Efficient Methods track: natural fit for structured pruning + reasoning model recovery\\\\n- Reasoning model compression is timely (DeepSeek-R1, QwQ, etc. driving demand)\\\\n- Empirical rigor + mechanistic analysis aligns with EMNLP's preference for thorough experimentation\\\\n\\\\n## Venue Fit Risks\\\\n- **\\\\\\\"Just another pruning metric\\\\\\\"**: Mitigate with Redundancy Paradox framing, LTH generalization (paradigm-conditioned trainability), and mechanistic analysis showing WHY it works\\\\n- **\\\\\\\"Single model\\\\\\\"**: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B is the most widely-used open reasoning model; multi-sparsity + multi-method comparison compensates\\\\n- **\\\\\\\"MPruner already uses CKA\\\\\\\"**: Different granularity (intra-layer per-head vs inter-layer), different objective (recoverability prediction vs redundancy removal), different domain (reasoning LLM vs CNN/general transformer)\\\\n- **\\\\\\\"Cross-component pruning not observed\\\\\\\"**: At 20-25% sparsity, only MLP groups are pruned (0 attention groups). Framework scores both types jointly, but global ranking at moderate sparsity naturally prioritizes MLP removal. Mitigate by: (1) honest description of actual pruning distribution, (2) noting the CKA signal drives recovery gap via MLP group reranking, (3) optionally test higher sparsity where attention groups enter pruning range\\\\n\\\\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Experimental Responses\\\\n\\\\n| Concern | Response | Supporting Experiment |\\\\n|---------|----------|----------------------|\\\\n| Incremental over importance-only pruning | Post-prune gap is modest (4pp), but RLVR recovery gap is decisive; structure selection matters more for recoverability than for immediate accuracy | exp-001, exp-002 |\\\\n| CKA overlap might correlate with simpler metrics | Scoring ablation: CKA vs magnitude/gradient/random | exp-007 |\\\\n| Single model generalization | Multi-sparsity (20%, 25%, 30%) + multi-method (Standard, GRASPrune, RASP) | exp-003, exp-005 |\\\\n| RLVR vs SFT claim needs controlled comparison | Same pruned models, same data budget, different recovery method | exp-006 |\\\\n| Statistical rigor of correlation claim | Mixed-effects regression with covariates on MLP groups (N=784, ~200 pruned) | exp-008 |\\\\n| Only MLP groups pruned at 20% sparsity | Honest description + CKA drives recovery gap via MLP reranking + optional higher sparsity test | experiments.tex |\\\\n| Recovery might just reflect post-prune accuracy | Include GRASPrune (different post-prune accuracy profile) to break correlation | exp-005 |\\\\n\\\\n## Key Differentiations\\\\n- **vs MPruner (2024)**: inter-layer CKA for depth pruning in CNNs → RASP uses intra-layer CKA between individual heads for width pruning in reasoning LLMs, optimizing for post-recovery (not immediate) performance\\\\n- **vs Self-Healing (2025)**: tests RLVR recovery with standard pruning → RASP optimizes the pruning decision FOR recovery\\\\n- **vs RESP (Dec 2025)**: reasoning-trace calibration without recovery → RASP includes recovery-awareness in the pruning score\\\\n- **vs GRASPrune (ACL 2026)**: SOTA budgeted pruning without recovery study → GRASPrune is our primary baseline\\\\n- **vs PASER (2025)**: optimizes recovery DATA → RASP optimizes pruning STRUCTURE (complementary)\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 8449, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JjoCkoWmGvH77iEv5CoXPc","session_id":"e50da390-5c7e-4dcd-8358-bec3c8329c08","uuid":"95991bf2-600e-4844-bef5-7709cfb10073","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:59:54.822Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FWZyEC6hmEu1orHZWS6ASp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Np8dg4xCyjmFJPRcGJyF1S","name":"mcp__agent-ml-research__read_project_file","input":{"project":"recovery_aware_struct_prune","file":"memory.md","max_chars":0},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2300,"cache_read_input_tokens":16965,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2300,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":70,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JjoCkoWmGvH77iEv5CoXPc","session_id":"e50da390-5c7e-4dcd-8358-bec3c8329c08","uuid":"33cca1d1-c476-473d-9a50-945426017dfc"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Np8dg4xCyjmFJPRcGJyF1S","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/memory.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Memory\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-05-15: D022 — Calibration sensitivity at 20% sparsity (fragile threshold)\\\\n- [关键发现] westb (512 calibration samples) 和 westd (256 samples) 代码完全一致（0 行 diff），但 α=0.0 结果分别为 1% 和 30%。根因：calibration sample 数量差异导致 ~5% MLP group 选择不同。模型在 20% sparsity 处于 fragile threshold，少量 group 变化引起巨大 accuracy 差异。\\\\n- [验证] westb Standard 1% 是真实退化（输出 \\\\\\\"10 years, 10 years...\\\\\\\" 重复循环 316KB），不是 eval bug。同服务器、同脚本、间隔 45 分钟，RASP 输出连贯推理（91KB）。\\\\n- [α ablation N=100] α=0.0 (30%) / α=0.5 (25%) / α=1.0 (27%) — 95% CI 重叠，无统计显著差异。需要 N=1319 全集才能下结论。\\\\n- [行动项] westd 需用 n_samples=512 重算 importance scores 消除 calibration 混淆。\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-05-15: GRPO sampling collapse on pruned models\\\\n- [失败模式] SFT 恢复 greedy 准确率 (57-64%) 和 EOS (99%) 后，GRPO sampling (temp=0.7) 仍导致剪枝模型退化为重复循环，grad_norm=0, reward=0。根因：剪枝模型在 stochastic sampling 下脆弱。\\\\n- [v2 失败] beta=0 + max_completion_length=1024, 双组 step 30-35 collapse → GRPO method failure。\\\\n- [v3 失败] beta=0.01 触发 GRPOTrainer from_pretrained 加载 ref_model，剪枝模型 shape mismatch 崩溃。\\\\n- [v4 修复] monkey-patch create_model_from_path → load_pruned_model。temp 0.7→0.4, repetition_penalty=1.15, format_reward +0.1, gradient_checkpointing=True, max_completion_length=2048。TRL 1.1.0。\\\\n- [经验] GRPO 在剪枝模型上必须预检 sampling 生成质量。beta>0 需要手动处理 ref_model 加载。\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-05-15: GraSP vs RASP — gradient saliency 远劣于 CKA-aware pruning\\\\n- [关键发现] GraSP 20% post-prune accuracy = 8% (50 样本 checkpoint)，RASP 20% = 29-31%，3.6x 差距。\\\\n- GraSP 模型 EOS rate 仅 2%（几乎所有输出截断在 4096 token），说明 gradient-based saliency 在结构化剪枝中严重破坏生成能力。\\\\n- 使用 GRASPrune 库，keep_ratio=0.80, rescale_alpha=0.5, 512 samples, 4 epochs gate training。\\\\n- 模型路径: `/root/autodl-tmp/recovery_aware_struct_prune/pruned_graspune_20/`\\\\n- [意义] 有力回应 Dream reviewer concern (plan_005)——RASP 显著优于主流 gradient-based baseline。\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-05-15: α ablation SFT — 非单调关系确认\\\\n- α=4.0: post-prune 40% → post-SFT 62% (+22pp)，为所有 α 值中最高\\\\n- α=1.0 (RASP default): post-prune 29% → post-SFT 57%\\\\n- Standard: post-prune 27% → post-SFT 64%\\\\n- [观察] post-prune 阶段 α=4.0 最优，但 post-SFT 阶段差距缩小（57-64% 范围）。SFT 有均衡化效应。\\\\n- [关键问题] GRPO 阶段是否能拉开差距？这是整个论文 narrative 的决定性验证。\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-05-15: sft_standard_20 checkpoint 已删除\\\\n- 磁盘清理删除了 sft_standard_20（81GB），正在 cuda:1 重训。\\\\n- 重训参数：pruned_standard_20 + GSM8K full train (7473) + 2 epochs + lr=2e-5，~37-40 min。\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-05-15: 代码与环境备忘\\\\n- α ablation: `prune.py` 支持 `--alpha`，CKA 分数缓存 `results/cka_scores.pt`\\\\n- Full eval: `scripts/run_full_eval.sh`（新版），`src/run_full_eval.sh`（旧版）\\\\n- GRASPrune: `/root/GRASPrune/`，不要 `pip install -r requirements.txt`\\\\n- GRPO 输出路径：`grpo_stage2_rasp_20` / `grpo_stage2_standard_20`\\\\n- sft_recovery.py 不支持 `--save_strategy` 和 `--overwrite_output_dir` 参数\\\\n- westb 磁盘：数据盘 250GB 已用 141GB，剩 110GB\\\\n- westd 磁盘：释放 93GB 后空间充足（原 72GB used → 大幅改善）\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 2685, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JjoCkoWmGvH77iEv5CoXPc","session_id":"e50da390-5c7e-4dcd-8358-bec3c8329c08","uuid":"8e85a95d-054f-4f01-809f-0a45ff04b19d","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:59:55.088Z"}
